Relevant columns and their potential usage
• ZIP_CODES."zip_code": 5‑digit postal code; used for final grouping and ranking.  
• ZIP_CODES."zip_code_geom": polygon for each ZIP; used with ST_WITHIN to spatially assign each storm event to a ZIP code.  
• STORMS_20XX."event_type": filter to hail events (value normally equals ‘HAIL’ – case may vary).  
• STORMS_20XX."event_point": POINT geometry (lon/lat) for each event; used in the ST_WITHIN spatial join.  
• STORMS_20XX."event_begin_time": numeric timestamp; restrict to the most recent 10 calendar years (2014‑01‑01 → 2024‑12‑31).  
• (optional) STORMS_20XX."event_latitude", "event_longitude": quick sanity checks before using geometries.  
Conditions that will be useful  
• WHERE "event_type" ILIKE '%hail%'  
• WHERE "event_begin_time" >= 1388534400000000   -- ≈ 2014‑01‑01 in microseconds (validate actual units first)  
• ST_WITHIN( s."event_point", z."zip_code_geom" )  

